<HEAD><style>/* Lecture Hall — enlarged textbook figures. Palette and type route through theme variables. */
.gml-card {
  --lh-ink: var(--heading-color);
  --lh-signal: var(--accent-color);
  --lh-field: var(--card-color);
  --lh-soft: var(--surface-color);
  --lh-rule: var(--neutral-border-color);
  --lh-line: 1.5pt;
  --lh-radius: 6pt;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.gml-card p.gml-paragraph,
.gml-card .gml-table__cell,
.gml-card .gml-heading { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.gml-card h3.gml-heading,
.gml-card h4.gml-heading { font-family: var(--body-font); }

/* Signature 1: the calm chalk field that holds every construction. */
.lh-chalk-field.gml-grid,
.lh-chalk-field.gml-grid-cell { --cell-default-bg: var(--lh-field); }

/* Signature 2: monumental projection type; scale comes from the theme ledger. */
.lh-monumental.gml-display,
.lh-monumental.gml-heading {
  letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  line-height: 0.95;
  text-wrap: balance;
}

/* Signature 3: exactly one authored teaching signal per construction. */
.lh-signal { --lh-signal-role: var(--lh-signal); }

/* Signature 4: large numbered lecture callouts with a single marker channel. */
.lh-callouts {
  --marker-inline-size: 34pt;
  --marker-gap: 12pt;
  --marker-color: var(--lh-ink);
  --marker-border-color: var(--lh-ink);
  --marker-border-width: 1.5pt;
  --grid-divider-color: var(--lh-rule);
  --grid-divider-width: 1px;
}

/* Signature 5: narrow subject figure rail; no radius or decorative plate. */
.lh-figure-rail.gml-grid-cell {
  --cell-radius: 0;
  min-width: 0;
}
.lh-figure-rail .gml-image { --figure-radius: 0; }

/* Signature 6: two-column image cargo with one deliberate seam grammar. */
.lh-figure-grid {
  --grid-divider-color: var(--lh-rule);
  --grid-divider-width: 1px;
  --grid-seam-inset: 0;
  --figure-radius: var(--lh-radius);
}

/* Signature 7: hero and divider imagery stays quiet behind monumental copy. */
.lh-image-break.gml-image { --figure-radius: 0; }

/* Signature 8: evidence images read as inspectable plates, not decoration. */
.lh-inspection-plate.gml-grid,
.lh-inspection-plate.gml-grid-cell {
  --grid-divider-color: var(--lh-rule);
  --grid-divider-width: 1px;
  --figure-radius: var(--lh-radius);
}

/* Native data remains a flat teaching instrument. */
.gml-chart {
  --gamma-chart-figure-background: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-background: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-border-color: transparent;
  --gamma-chart-grid-color: var(--lh-rule);
  --gamma-chart-grid-dasharray: 0;
  --gamma-chart-axis-line-color: var(--lh-ink);
  --gamma-chart-origin-line-color: var(--lh-ink);
  --gamma-chart-font-family: var(--body-font);
  --gamma-chart-text-color: var(--body-color);
  --gamma-chart-secondary-text-color: var(--body-color-muted);
  --gamma-chart-bar-rx: 0;
  --gamma-chart-bar-ry: 0;
  --gamma-chart-line-width: 3px;
  --gamma-chart-line-cap: square;
  --gamma-chart-area-opacity: 0.15;
  --gamma-chart-pie-stroke: var(--card-color);
  --gamma-chart-pie-stroke-width: 3px;
}

/* Restored native evidence-family hooks. */
.comparison-table {
  --table-border-color: var(--lh-ink);
  --table-border-width: 1.5px;
  --table-cell-padding: 12pt 14pt;
  --table-header-bg: transparent;
  --table-stripe-bg: transparent;
  --table-radius: 0;
}
.two-column-compare .gml-table__cell:first-child { width: 36%; }


/* People are organized around the human subject, not repeated as a figure-plus-ledger split. */
.lh-role-constellation,
.lh-role-stack {
  --grid-divider-color: var(--lh-rule);
  --grid-divider-width: 1px;
  --cell-icon-size: 28pt;
  --marker-color: var(--lh-ink);
  --marker-border-color: var(--lh-ink);
}</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="DWsGdSgC_E" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="nQLZFz0fG1" vertical-align="center" colspan="29"><p role="eyebrow">Agricultural tools and machinery (alsintan)</p><display size="md" font-size="49pt" class="lh-monumental">The efficiency of agricultural machinery:<br>why <span text-color="accent">utilization</span> beats horsepower</display></grid-item><grid-item id="YYlEVQxgcO" class="lh-image-break" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="31"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/qKUY8pUZ_TBfN6LoFxj51.png" saved-media-id="8j1lsz8sujquq4t" source="image.ai-generated" width="470pt" height="410pt" image-style="lecture-spot" alt="Spot-color technical line drawing of one complete walk-behind rice transplanter moving across a shallow puddled paddy, operator guiding the handles, seedling trays and planting mechanism clearly visible, restrained natural green and red accents, isolated on a pale ground, no text, labels, logos, brand marks, numerals, or interface readouts" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1536,&quot;height&quot;:1024,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:true}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0VwgC32Mct"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="l6T5ix4f8H"><h2 class="lh-monumental">A machine that sits idle is more expensive than no machine at all</h2><p>Purchase price and engine power do not reveal the cost of work. Annual ownership cost stays fixed; cost per hectare falls only when the calendar supplies more hectares.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="SsRKqVRlhK" align="center" vertical-align="center" cell-style="outline" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">20 ha/year</p><display size="md" font-size="52pt" class="lh-monumental">Rp 1,023,000</display><p role="caption" align="center">per hectare</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Fy-PF7GIFj" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="12"><h3 align="center"><span text-color="accent">Same machine</span></h3><p role="caption" align="center">Different calendar</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-W9SdmuipE" align="center" vertical-align="center" cell-style="outline" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">45 ha/year</p><display size="md" font-size="52pt" class="lh-monumental"><span text-color="accent">Rp 666,000</span></display><p role="caption" align="center">per hectare</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">This deck builds the arithmetic, then follows one reproducible case from purchase decision to seasonal use. Ownership-cost method: <a href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/budgeting-farm-machinery-costs">Ontario Ministry of Agriculture</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5Q4bjOEP45" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="j3z-b14Lav"><h2 class="lh-monumental">“Efficiency” hides three separate questions. Measure all three.</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="2KfGBTKx9a" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/g1cIIVXMSlH1h8grfToE.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="tractor working field clock" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black shape of a tractor with minimal details, set against a white background, conveying the concept of agriculture or farming machinery.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Field efficiency</h3><p>What share of field time is actual work rather than turning, refilling, clearing or waiting?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="T-UriN0Zd7" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/WAH9SGZyBbxSPkCy5sqiug.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="farm machinery operating cost" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A minimalist silhouette of a farmhouse or a barn with a silo, embodying the concept of a rural farm or agricultural land.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Cost efficiency</h3><p>What is the real fixed-plus-variable cost per hectare at your annual use?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="GdasX-jwVL" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/CWoZw8wMw76hzAHan9vyNt.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="grain sack and farm worker" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black grain silhouette against a white background, representing the concept of grain.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Loss and labor</h3><p>How much grain is saved and how many work hours are released per hectare?</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="16pt"></spacer><h3 align="center"><span text-color="accent">High capacity can still fail when the machine is chronically underused.</span></h3><p role="caption" align="center">Methods: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/AgDM/crops/pdf/a3-24.pdf">field capacity</a> · <a href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/budgeting-farm-machinery-costs">machinery cost</a> · <a href="https://epublikasi.pertanian.go.id/berkala/jae/article/view/3633">harvest loss</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="blu0qYkX6O"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="2Q1EMwtr7R"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Field capacity: the one formula the rest of the deck rests on</h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="vgulgo-5Qv" vertical-align="center" cell-style="outline" colspan="29"><p role="eyebrow">Theoretical capacity</p><formula>C_t=\frac{v\;(\mathrm{km/h})\times w\;(\mathrm{m})}{10}\quad \mathrm{ha/h}</formula><p role="eyebrow">Effective capacity</p><formula>C_e=C_t\times \eta_f</formula><p>Field efficiency <math>\eta_f</math> includes headland turns, refuelling and refilling.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="fKruPxeqmY" vertical-align="center" colspan="31"><p role="eyebrow">Worked subsoiler example</p><p>Speed 5 km/h · width 2 m · 17% of time lost · field efficiency 0.83.</p><formula>\frac{5\times2}{10}\times0.83=0.83\ \mathrm{ha/h}</formula><formula>0.83\times10=8.3\ \mathrm{ha/day}</formula><p role="caption">The arithmetic shows the inputs, operation and result on one line.</p></grid-item></grid><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="UV1qkYPD-7" align="center" colspan="20"><p align="center"><b>Plows</b><br>78–85%</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nnPhec35qe" align="center" colspan="20"><p align="center"><b>Tandem disk</b><br>about 80–83%</p></grid-item><grid-item id="SoCvVWWZ0Q" align="center" colspan="20"><p align="center"><b>Fertilizer spreader</b><br>about 70%</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Capacity method and example: <a href="https://www.nda.gov.za/images/Branches/Economica%20Development%20Trade%20and%20Marketing/Statistc%20and%20%20Economic%20Analysis/economic-analysis/2015-2016-guide-to-machinery-costs-field-capacity-explain-table-.pdf">machinery-cost guide</a>. Typical efficiencies: <a href="https://www.computus.co.za/Publikasies/machA1.pdf">Computus table</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="p3ZRASGkQQ" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="8E6bRAeOjU" padding-bottom="24pt"><h2 class="lh-monumental">A measured Indonesian machine: the Indo Jarwo transplanter at <span text-color="accent">86%</span></h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="NWmtKQvzBV" align="center" vertical-align="center" cell-style="outline" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="88pt" class="lh-monumental"><span text-color="accent">86%</span></display><h3 role="subheading" align="center">Field efficiency</h3><p align="center">0.12 ÷ 0.14</p><p role="caption" align="center">8.33 hours to plant one hectare</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-_Ag9nwuvT" class="lh-inspection-plate" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/qt88O-hg5KD-cnXd053Tr.png" saved-media-id="hv9d11x3a9dq34w" source="image.ai-generated" width="570pt" height="248pt" image-style="lecture-spot" alt="Spot-color technical line drawing of one complete Indo-style jajar legowo rice transplanter in side view on a measured puddled paddy plot, operator walking behind, seedling trays, wheels and planting arms clearly visible, restrained natural green with one red accent, isolated on pale inspection ground, no text, labels, logos, brand marks, numerals, or interface readouts" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1536,&quot;height&quot;:1024,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:true}"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="vj8RSnimeK" align="center" colspan="20"><p align="center"><b>1.52 km/h</b><br><span font-size="16pt">best speed</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="ynaKsMo-Jc" align="center" colspan="20"><p align="center"><b>0.14 ha/h</b><br><span font-size="16pt">theoretical</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="eRb9oM0L-i" align="center" colspan="20"><p align="center"><b>0.12 ha/h</b><br><span font-size="16pt">effective</span></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Pinrang, South Sulawesi: three speeds on 10 × 10 m plots. <a href="https://jurnal.fp.unila.ac.id/index.php/JTP/article/download/4851/pdf">Field study</a>. A separate BBP Mektan manual transplanter reached 86.79%, with 4.2% of time lost. Reproduce the measure: time one pass, measure width, count turns.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4m_s0uLZG7"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="PBKTsjMmwo"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Where the missing <span text-color="accent">14%</span> goes, and which parts you can buy back</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="LRh01uIvcH" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/g1cIIVXMSlH1h8grfToE.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="tractor turning at field headland" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black shape of a tractor with minimal details, set against a white background, conveying the concept of agriculture or farming machinery.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Headland turning</h4><p font-size="17pt">Usually the largest loss. Longer runs and squarer plots reduce it.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sD92cp99gf" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/H7D7SU2G9cQfUQGZ7Mronn.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="seedling trays staged beside field" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A sprouting plant with two leaves grows from a half-circle base, symbolizing the concept of a seedling.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Refilling</h4><p font-size="17pt">Stage trays or tanks at the headland, not beside the road.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="WHc2-9ww3o" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/WAH9SGZyBbxSPkCy5sqiug.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="farm machine clearing blockage wrench" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A minimalist silhouette of a farmhouse or a barn with a silo, embodying the concept of a rural farm or agricultural land.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Adjustment</h4><p font-size="17pt">Fast setup and blockage clearing are operator skills that can be trained.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="KIwuKAhxB9" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/QKmUS9t5DxBZ2BRpNpM7PM.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="tractor transport between fragmented plots" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black silhouette of a riding lawn mower with a seat and a steering wheel, symbolizing lawn care and outdoor maintenance equipment.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Plot transport</h4><p font-size="17pt">Travel is not field time, but it still consumes the working day.</p></grid-item></grid><h3 align="center"><span text-color="accent">Plot geometry and logistics set most of the loss. The engine does not.</span></h3></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4jWVM40pLI" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="O9ibCPXYse"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Five stages of use, each with its own efficiency trap</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill" class="lh-callouts" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="2U8CihtdZZ" colspan="12"><h4>Land preparation</h4><p font-size="15pt">Hand tractor output reached up to 15× manual hoeing in measured trials.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3v2IOkDBIG" colspan="12"><h4>Planting</h4><p font-size="15pt">Manual: 32.79 male + 23.79 female h/ha. Mechanized: 18.67 male h/ha.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5pY_HMZE3A" colspan="12"><h4>Crop care</h4><p font-size="15pt">Power weeder output measured about 10× manual weeding.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="essinsqiWy" colspan="12"><h4>Harvest</h4><p font-size="15pt">A combine used three workers and about five hours per hectare.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gN6PptMvYY" colspan="12"><h4><span text-color="accent">Post-harvest</span></h4><p font-size="15pt">Thresher output measured about 17× manual processing.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Sources: <a href="https://repository.pertanian.go.id/bitstreams/3b4f6e92-594f-4dda-820e-e45545382b3b/download">land preparation, crop care and threshing</a> · <a href="https://doi.org/10.20961/sepa.v10i1.13958">planting labor</a> · <a href="https://repository.ummat.ac.id/6179/">combine harvest</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="trw56t_TfN"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="QuQNX0lmYr" padding-bottom="22pt"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Six checks before buying farm machinery</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="14pt 18pt"><grid-item id="0q7m9-yD0_" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/febDHXhqgKnpkiMkvigQve.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="tractor engine power load"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Heaviest task</h4><p font-size="17pt">Undersized units finish late; size power for peak demand.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="b5X3QjqNom" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Z4NDxa6SgdRGPgJVNZjT.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="fragmented agricultural field plots map"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Plot geometry</h4><p font-size="17pt">Fragmented plots cap efficiency, whatever the machine cost.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="eVFVfWIcaL" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/WUbwApYuudoQYbqegJZtPu.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="paddy soil water traction"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Soil and water</h4><p font-size="17pt">Puddled paddy, dry upland and peat require different traction.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="TiHSB1bOea" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/dCHpKHGSHFAcYaB75V3W.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="farm calendar hectares annual area"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Annual area</h4><p font-size="17pt">Compare available hectares with the break-even area.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1YhPVz2irl" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/WAH9SGZyBbxSPkCy5sqiug.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="farm machinery mechanic spare parts"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Local support</h4><p font-size="17pt">Local service, parts and operator skill are essential.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="8kzG9nR7Cg" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/QKmUS9t5DxBZ2BRpNpM7PM.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="tractor custom hire agreement"></icon></grid-item-label><h4><span text-color="accent">Hire alternative</span></h4><p font-size="17pt">Hire when local custom rates beat per-hectare ownership cost.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Decision methods: <a href="http://arhiva.nara.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1591">break-even area</a> · <a href="https://farmdocdaily.illinois.edu/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/fdd010917.pdf">own-versus-hire comparison</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VkpgIaLVRN" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="K-iTPvU98x" padding-bottom="24pt"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Fixed cost spreads; variable cost tracks use</h2><grid divider="2pt palette-2" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="kvIVejBb_-" background-color="surface" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Fixed ownership cost</p><h3>Unchanged at 5 ha or 50 ha</h3><p>Depreciation, interest, insurance and housing are paid each year.</p><formula>D=\frac{\text{purchase price}-\text{salvage value}}{\text{years of optimal life}}</formula></grid-item><grid-item id="WinBP_qvFC" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Variable operating cost</p><h3>Roughly constant per hectare</h3><p>Fuel, lubricant, repairs and operator wages rise with work completed.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="10pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="aMoXS5EfwY" background-color="palette-2" align="center" padding="16pt 24pt"><formula>C_{\mathrm{ha}}=\frac{F_{\mathrm{annual}}}{A_{\mathrm{annual}}}+V_{\mathrm{ha}}</formula><p align="center">The denominator is the whole argument. More hectares divide the same annual fixed cost.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Cost definitions and straight-line depreciation: <a href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/budgeting-farm-machinery-costs">Ontario machinery-cost guide</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="2FacjLuHFY"><grid divider="2pt palette-2"><grid-item id="jIGKNO-73N" background-color="palette-2" vertical-align="center" colspan="24"><h2 font-size="32pt" class="lh-monumental">Break-even area: buy or hire</h2><p role="eyebrow">Decision rule</p><formula>A_{\mathrm{BE}}=\frac{F_{\mathrm{annual}}}{R_{\mathrm{custom}}-V_{\mathrm{ha}}}</formula><p>Below break-even, owning costs more per hectare than hiring. <b>Measured Sijunjung case:</b> Rp 325,057/ha with a modified manual transplanter versus Rp 653,343/ha for manual planting.</p><display size="md" font-size="38pt" class="lh-monumental"><span text-color="accent">13.46 ha/year</span></display><p role="caption"><a href="http://repository.pertanian.go.id/handle/123456789/2046?show=full">Measured case</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="F2Y3K72AjI" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative transplanter cost curve</p><graph chart-type="line" y-axis-min="0" text-size="lg" config="{&quot;appearance&quot;:{&quot;customSeriesColors&quot;:{&quot;series1&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;var(--accent-color)&quot;},&quot;series2&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;var(--neutral-border-color)&quot;},&quot;series3&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;var(--heading-color)&quot;}}},&quot;legend&quot;:{&quot;position&quot;:&quot;top&quot;}}" width="500pt" height="270pt"><properties><property key="area" label="Hectares per year" type="label"></property><property key="fixed" label="Fixed cost per ha (Rp '000)" type="data"></property><property key="variable" label="Variable cost per ha (Rp '000)" type="data"></property><property key="total" label="Total cost per ha (Rp '000)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>10</cell><cell>1286</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>1666</cell></row><row><cell>20</cell><cell>643</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>1023</cell></row><row><cell>30</cell><cell>429</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>809</cell></row><row><cell>40</cell><cell>322</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>702</cell></row><row><cell>50</cell><cell>257</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>637</cell></row><row><cell>60</cell><cell>214</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>594</cell></row></data></graph><p role="caption">Fixed cost per hectare collapses with use. Variable cost stays flat, so the total falls steeply and then flattens.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ToimeGnpnY"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="EfOyeRPFDP"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Harvest loss is efficiency you can weigh in the sack</h2><table col-widths="[18,41,41]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="comparison-table"><tbody><tr><td><p>Study</p></td><td><p>Measured loss</p></td><td><p>Cost or interpretation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt"><b>Banten</b></p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Combine harvesters cut loss by <b>200.39 kg/ha</b>, about <b>3.52% of yield</b>.</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Matched-sample result. <a href="https://epublikasi.pertanian.go.id/berkala/jae/article/view/3633">Study</a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt"><b>Sumbawa</b></p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Combine 0.43%/ha versus manual 1.03%/ha.</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Rp 9.33 million/ha versus Rp 11.27 million/ha. <a href="https://eprints.unram.ac.id/31651/">Study</a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt"><b>North Sulawesi</b></p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Kubota DC70 Plus total loss 4.9%.</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">4.7% was scattered during cutting alone. <a href="https://ejournal.unsrat.ac.id/v3/index.php/teta/article/download/51068/44083/121028">Trial</a></p></td></tr></tbody></table><aside variant="caution"><p><b>Define the boundary before comparing machines.</b> These studies count different stages and types of loss.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="dczUA2m8TM"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Rq47l3LrGx"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Seven indicators worth tracking every season</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="NntmYW_AWA" padding-right="22pt" colspan="30"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="outline" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" spacing="none" class="lh-callouts"><grid-item id="iZ5cmflg0a"><p><b>Effective field capacity</b> · actual area ÷ actual field hours, in ha/hour.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="tFnsQsz6Y3"><p><b>Field efficiency</b> · effective capacity ÷ theoretical capacity, in percent.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ILjzMR-Ky5"><p><b>Utilization</b> · hectares per year, compared directly with break-even area.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="S3vWH-wo17"><p><b>Cost per hectare</b> · fixed plus variable cost, recalculated annually.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="TlFvOw30pa" padding-left="22pt" colspan="30"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="outline" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-start="5" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" spacing="none" class="lh-callouts"><grid-item id="WOtu52RYU-"><p><b>Harvest or process loss</b> · weighed, not estimated.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cZMNM88Q8e"><p><b>Fuel per hectare</b> · an early warning of a maintenance problem.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FBZanujX6O"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Downtime</b></span> · percent of scheduled days when work stops.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Capacity definitions: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/AgDM/crops/pdf/a3-24.pdf">Iowa State machinery management guide</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ivruUuoixs"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="0diTJbSBjZ"><h2 font-size="33pt" class="lh-monumental">Case study: UPJA Tani Makmur buys a transplanter</h2><p role="caption"><b>Illustrative fictional farmer-group service unit; figures are constructed for reproducibility, not drawn from a real cooperative.</b></p><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="d-chCOzVMt" vertical-align="center" colspan="34"><table col-widths="[52,48]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 6pt 10pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Input</p></td><td><p>Annual result</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt">Rp 75,000,000 machine · 8-year life · 10% salvage</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt"><b>Rp 8,437,500/year depreciation</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt">8% × Rp 41,250,000 average investment</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Rp 3,300,000/year</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt">Housing and insurance</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Rp 1,125,000/year</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt"><b>Annual fixed cost</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p font-size="17pt"><b>Rp 12,862,500/year</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="17pt">Fuel, oil, two operators and repairs</p></td><td><p font-size="17pt">Rp 380,000/ha</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="MFTgFCH4Ph" vertical-align="center" cell-style="outline" colspan="26"><p role="eyebrow">Local custom rate</p><h3>Rp 700,000/ha</h3><formula>\frac{12{,}862{,}500}{700{,}000-380{,}000}=40.2\ \mathrm{ha/year}</formula><p role="eyebrow">Year one: 20 ha served</p><display size="md" font-size="36pt" class="lh-monumental"><span text-color="accent">Rp 1,023,000/ha</span></display><p>Ownership cost exceeded the rate charged.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Straight-line depreciation method: <a href="https://files.ontario.ca/omafra-budgeting-farm-machinery-costs-20-007-en-2020-05-12.pdf">Ontario machinery-cost worksheet</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="_3iLWgtOqG" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jCkInqbHAX"><h2 class="lh-monumental">The calendar, not the machine, was the binding constraint</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="8HF9BFYNKW" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 18pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">One village</p><h3 font-size="20pt">6 h/day · 20-day window · 2 seasons</h3><formula>0.12\times6=0.72\ \mathrm{ha/day}</formula><formula>0.72\times20\times2=\mathbf{28.8}\ \mathrm{ha/year}</formula><p>Before delays, annual capacity was below the 40.2 ha/year break-even.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PaY8RewmBy" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 18pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Three villages</p><h3 font-size="20pt">8 h/day · 25-day window · 2 seasons</h3><formula>0.12\times8=0.96\ \mathrm{ha/day}</formula><formula>0.96\times25\times2=\mathbf{48}\ \mathrm{ha/year}</formula><p>Staggered planting dates widened access to working days.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="BJbfRkM74K" background-color="palette-2" padding="12pt 20pt"><p align="center"><b>At 45 ha:</b> Rp 666,000/ha—below the Rp 700,000/ha custom rate. <span text-color="accent">No new horsepower was purchased.</span></p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Measured machine capacity: <a href="https://jurnal.fp.unila.ac.id/index.php/JTP/article/download/4851/pdf">0.12 ha/hour in the Pinrang field test</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="nbliOOJrrz"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="z89VlH9ZBt" padding-bottom="24pt"><h2 class="lh-monumental">Five strategies ranked by return per rupiah spent</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="outline" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="fill" padding="8pt 12pt" class="lh-callouts"><grid-item id="7HsxYewOqr" colspan="30"><h4><span text-color="accent">Raise utilization first</span></h4><p>Share UPJA services across villages with staggered planting dates. More hectares shrink fixed cost per hectare.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YlsWw9l8xb" colspan="30"><h4>Train operators</h4><p>Turning discipline, correct adjustment and quick blockage clearing recover field time at near-zero capital cost.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="QaLPPjrA4-" colspan="30"><h4>Prevent downtime</h4><p>Scheduled servicing protects the working days on which break-even depends.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cOEukkpyNe" colspan="30"><h4>Right-size capacity</h4><p>Extra output that the planting or harvest calendar cannot use becomes pure fixed cost.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="2Ln6Jn11hr" colspan="60"><h4>Measure and record</h4><p>Your own effective field capacity beats a brochure figure. <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/AgDM/crops/pdf/a3-24.pdf">Method</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="WRnnNubxM0" vertical-align="center"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="d4OQhBKz5g" class="lh-chalk-field" vertical-align="center" padding-right="30pt" colspan="29"><h2 class="lh-monumental">What to take back to the field</h2><p>Efficiency is a ratio you compute, not a quality the machine possesses.</p><ul><li>Field efficiency of 80–86% is realistic and measurable.</li><li>Annual use governs cost per hectare; break-even area decides buy or hire.</li><li>Mechanization pays through loss avoided and labor released, not speed alone.</li></ul><p role="caption">Evidence: <a href="https://jurnal.fp.unila.ac.id/index.php/JTP/article/download/4851/pdf">transplanter efficiency</a> · <a href="https://eprints.unram.ac.id/31651/">harvest loss and cost</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="X1ZXMN7cFA" vertical-align="center" padding-left="30pt" colspan="31"><p role="eyebrow">First action</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="syp6Wyhk1Z" colspan="20"><h4>Time one pass</h4><p>Calculate effective capacity and field efficiency.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Bl7SysyXxN" colspan="20"><h4>Weigh one loss sample</h4><p>Record grain or process loss using a defined boundary.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="neG7Ts8ES3" colspan="20"><h4><span text-color="accent">Compare the rate</span></h4><p>Put your cost per hectare beside the local custom-hire rate.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>